    <briefdescription>
<para>Get or create a thread-local cache instance. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Get or create a thread-local cache instance.Returns a reference to a thread-local cache singleton. Useful for high-performance scenarios where per-thread caching reduces lock contention. The thread-local cache is automatically created on first access and destroyed when the thread exits.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Reference to thread-local HKDFCache (never null) @thread_safe Yes - each thread gets its own instance </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Default configuration: 1000 entries, 300-second TTL</para>
</simplesect>
